Subject: [PATCH] libexec/mail: Date each message when it is delivered
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: uxkmwpoztvsyvpqoxqnxwlvvnoykqsqw
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:15:35 +0000

git format-patch dates each patch with its commit's author date, and
jj keeps that date across every rewrite, so a series posted today can
carry dates from days earlier. Delivery kept any Date it found, so
notmuch sorted those patches far from their cover letter and replies,
and recent work was hard to find.

A message now always carries its delivery time, which is also when it
reaches the list. A series is delivered in one burst, usually within a
second, and notmuch orders equal dates arbitrarily, so each delivery is
dated at least a second after the newest message in the maildir. The
series then sorts in the order it was delivered.

git am takes the author date from Date, so an applied patch is now
dated when it was posted, as with git send-email.
