change-id: uxkmwpoztvsyvpqoxqnxwlvvnoykqsqw

Root cause, from "[PATCH v3 0/6] Add just process-email": all seven
files were delivered at 1791997910 (17:11:50 UTC, the maildir file
names), but their Date headers read 17:11:01 for the cover (when
format-patch ran) and Sat 18:09:30 to Wed 10:08:26 for the patches.
Those are exactly the jj author timestamps of the commits, e.g.
ktpzmqru, authored 2026-10-10 18:09:30 and committed 2026-10-14.

Tested by delivering v3 and three replies into a scratch MAILDIR: each
got one Date, one second apart in delivery order. A folded Date header
is dropped whole, and a "Date:" line in the body is left alone.

One trade-off: a burst of N messages is dated up to N seconds ahead of
the wall clock, and a maildir file name from a host whose clock runs
fast pushes later deliveries after it.

